WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.717
GLM-5 .

00:00:01.529 --> 00:00:02.519
4 is Z

00:00:02.331 --> 00:00:02.767
.

00:00:02.638 --> 00:00:04.088
ai's first flagship

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:04.984
Loop Transformer

00:00:05.067 --> 00:00:06.446
reusing shared layers

00:00:06.966 --> 00:00:07.638
Z .

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:09.218
ai's GLM-5 .

00:00:09.030 --> 00:00:09.831
4 runs a

00:00:09.643 --> 00:00:10.904
block of 28

00:00:10.716 --> 00:00:12.390
weight-shared GLM-5

00:00:12.202 --> 00:00:13.369
layers twice per

00:00:13.181 --> 00:00:14.100
forward pass

00:00:14.301 --> 00:00:15.032
and says the

00:00:14.843 --> 00:00:17.296
750B-scale model reaches

00:00:17.108 --> 00:00:18.569
intelligence comparable

00:00:18.381 --> 00:00:20.279
to 2T-3T parameter

00:00:20.091 --> 00:00:20.786
models

00:00:21.310 --> 00:00:22.642
Instead of pre-training

00:00:22.466 --> 00:00:23.350
a looped model

00:00:23.161 --> 00:00:24.057
from scratch

00:00:24.305 --> 00:00:25.897
Z.ai adapted the

00:00:25.709 --> 00:00:27.831
pre-trained GLM-5 base

00:00:27.690 --> 00:00:29.093
through continued training

00:00:28.916 --> 00:00:29.647
so a group

00:00:29.470 --> 00:00:30.732
of 28 shared

00:00:30.544 --> 00:00:31.699
layers runs for

00:00:31.510 --> 00:00:32.607
two iterations

00:00:33.134 --> 00:00:34.655
Z.ai pitches it

00:00:34.526 --> 00:00:35.327
as the start

00:00:35.151 --> 00:00:36.612
of Generalized Coding

00:00:36.719 --> 00:00:37.650
and admits the

00:00:37.462 --> 00:00:38.428
model can get

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:39.336
stuck in overly

00:00:39.148 --> 00:00:40.692
long marathon thinking

00:00:40.516 --> 00:00:41.152
loops

